# Environment variables — website-studio
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development and fill in real
# values there. `.env.local` (and every other `.env*` file except this one)
# is git-ignored — see `.gitignore`. Never commit real secrets, keys, phone
# numbers, or email addresses. Every value below is a placeholder.

# --- Site URL --------------------------------------------------------------

# Required for a production build. Read by `app/layout.tsx` (drives
# `metadataBase`, which controls the canonical and OpenGraph URLs) and
# `app/robots.ts` (the `sitemap:` reference emitted in `robots.txt`).
#
# `lib/content/invariants.ts`'s `checkSiteUrlConfigured` deliberately FAILS a
# production build (`VERCEL_ENV=production`) if this is unset or still points
# at localhost — so nobody ships canonical/OG URLs pointing at
# `http://localhost:3000`. Non-production builds only warn.
#
# No production value has been decided yet — the plan is to use a Vercel
# subdomain until a custom domain is set up. The value below is an example
# shape, not a settled URL; replace it once the Vercel project exists.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app

# --- Brief form: email notification (lib/brief/notify.ts) ------------------

# Required for the brief form's email notification to send at all. Read by
# `lib/brief/notify.ts` via `fetch` against Resend's REST API
# (`https://api.resend.com/emails`). Without it, `sendBriefNotification()`
# logs an error and returns `{ ok: false, reason: "config" }` — the
# submission still validates, but no notification email goes out.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_resend_api_key

# Required. The mailbox that receives every brief submission. Read by
# `lib/brief/notify.ts`. Without it, sending fails the same way as a missing
# `RESEND_API_KEY` (config error, no email sent).
BRIEF_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Required. The "From" address Resend sends as. Read by
# `lib/brief/notify.ts`. IMPORTANT: this address's sending domain must be
# verified with Resend via DNS records (SPF/DKIM) before any send succeeds —
# until that verification is complete, every submission will fail at the
# provider, even with a correct API key and a syntactically valid address.
BRIEF_FROM_EMAIL=studio@example.com

# --- Brief form: abuse prevention (lib/brief/abuse.ts) ----------------------

# Required for the brief form's spam/abuse layer 1 (honeypot + HMAC-signed
# dwell-time check). Read by `lib/brief/abuse.ts` to sign and verify the
# hidden form token. This is a server-side secret you generate yourself
# (e.g. a random 32+ byte string) — it is not provided by any third party.
#
# Its absence makes abuse checking FAIL CLOSED, by design:
# `checkAbuseSignals()` cannot verify a signature against a secret that does
# not exist, so every submission is rejected rather than accepted
# unverified. Set this before the brief form goes live.
BRIEF_FORM_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string
